      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:36:1",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الرَّجُلِ يَشُكُّ وَ هُوَ قَائِمٌ لَا يَدْرِي رَكَعَ أَمْ لَمْ يَرْكَعْ قَالَ يَرْكَعُ وَ يَسْجُدُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Al Husayn Bin Saeed, from Fazalat Bin Ayoub, from Al Husayn Bin Usman, from Ibn Muskan, from Abu Baseer who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about the man who doubted and he was standing, not knowing whether he had performed the <span class=\"iTxt\">Rukū</span> or not. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘He should perform <span class=\"iTxt\">Rukū</span> and perform <span class=\"iTxt\">Sajdah</span>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from al-Husayn ibn Sa‘id from Fadalah ibn Ayyub from al-Husayn ibn ‘Uthman from ibn Muskan from abu Basir who has said the following: “I once asked abu ’Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about a man who in a standing position doubts and does not know if he has performed Ruku‘ (bowing down on one’s knees) or not. He (the Imam) said, ‘He performs Ruku‘ and Sajdah (prostration).”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
